Subject: [PATCH v11 0/8] jails/instances/lab-mail: Build the mail relay jail
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev

Agents need to send and read p7x.dev mail without holding the
Fastmail credentials. This series builds lab-mail, the relay jail
that holds them, and points lab-claude's mail clients at it.

Patch 1 is the spec. Patches 2 to 5 build lab-mail one service at a
time: the jail and its credential mount, smtprelay for sending,
mbsync for the append-only copy of the lists folder, and Dovecot to
serve that copy read-only over IMAP. Each one documents its part of
the mail flow in the README. Patch 6 gives each service a log file
of its own, and patch 7 adds just check, which reports whether each
part is set up and running. Patch 8 sets up msmtp, mbsync and a
separate notmuch profile in lab-claude, so the lab-devel list keeps
its jj maildir.

After applying, run just build and then restart lab-mail. The build
starts the jail before it installs the config, so only a restart
makes syslogd read the new routing, makes newsyslog create the log
files, and starts smtprelay with the fixed remotes.env. Then run
just check.

Testing. What I checked here, as fact:
- From lab-claude, earlier today, 127.0.0.1:2143 accepted a
  connection and 127.0.0.1:2525 refused one. Dovecot was up and
  smtprelay was not.
- v10's remotes.env, sourced after /etc/rc.subr with
  PATH=/sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin, as /etc/rc sets it at boot,
  printed "jq: not found" twice and built
  smtps://:@smtp.fastmail.com:465, a remote with no login. Under the
  same PATH, v11's builds
  smtps://me%40p7x.dev:p%40ss%3Aw%2Frd@smtp.fastmail.com:465.
- The fetch job, run against a scratch maildir with mbsync replaced
  by a command that adds two messages, printed "fetched 2 new
  messages" and made them readable by all. A second run that added
  nothing printed nothing.
- just 1.58 keeps the imported help as the default recipe and lists
  check beside the shared recipes. Where no lab-mail jail exists,
  just check prints "FAIL the jail is running" and exits 1.
- bsdtar creates /var/log/lab-mail from its type=dir entry in
  dist.mtree, with no such directory under dist/.
- Run unprivileged in lab-claude, the check prints one ok or FAIL
  line per check and exits 1. The shell files pass sh -n, and each
  dist.mtree lists exactly the files under dist/.

Inference, not tested:
- smtprelay is down because of the jq bug above. I cannot look inside
  lab-mail; its /var/log/maillog should say.
- syslogd routes by the tags smtprelay (from daemon -T),
  lab-mail-fetch (from logger -t), and dovecot (Dovecot's default
  syslog ident).
- service smtprelay status and service dovecot status work as
  rc.subr's status does for any script with a pidfile.
- smtprelay's default log level logs each session with its envelope
  and Fastmail's reply, and Dovecot's default logs each login.
- syslogd -s, the default, binds UDP port 514. lab-claude's syslogd
  holds *:514 now (fact, from sockstat), so lab-mail's could not
  bind it. lab-mail runs syslogd -ss, so the question does not arise.

Still as in v10: remotes.env runs for every smtprelay command, so a
broken mail-creds makes stop and status fail too, and mbsync does
not check the two lines itself. just check now reports an empty line
in mail-creds before either service hits it.

